@@s003 Compiler errors
@@s004 Each message below was obtained by <b>really compiling</b> with Scala 3.8.4 and the course options (<code>-Werror -source:future</code>). Many come from real attempts at the exercises. Search with <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>F</kbd> for the first line of the message you see.
@@s005 How to read "Found / Required"
@@s006 The most common message
@@s007 The code that does not work.
@@s008 <b>Found</b> = the type of what you wrote.
@@s009 <b>Required</b> = the type Scala expected at that point (here: the return type of <code>length</code>).
@@s010 The fix is always: to produce a value of the type <b>Required</b>.
